**Corollary 9.2 (presentation transfer, with its exact condition).** Theorems 2.3 and 9.1 apply to any other fixed faithful effective presentation which has finitely many charged descriptions at each finite budget and admits the finite-table compiler of §§3–8 with a computable *complete* charged bound. The existence proof uses only its finite description sets; the contradiction uses only that compiler. A semantic unrestricted-real class, an uncharged external service or the bare word “faithful” is not such a compiler theorem. An effective-horizon claim for a stricter subclass which excludes these observers needs its own analysis. In particular the constructed observers have large $p$ errors; nothing here rules out a procedure for a separately certified low-risk/near-optimal subclass.

